{"sourceSha256": "f22d04c38385a9ffd6ec6e82fa602ef51ef16e4568dfd0e1a4732462c89d58af", "text": "SETTING Emergency Room\n\nPATIENT You are a 25-year-old man/woman suffering fre m a headache. You have been suffering from a left-sided\nheadache since yesterday. The pain is \"pounding\" and is accompanied by nausea and vomiting. You have\nincreased sensinvity to light and sound,\n\nOver-the-counter painkiller has not been effective in allevianng the pain. You looked symptoms on some\n\nonline websites and found that your condition ts indicative of a migraine\n\nTASK When asked, tell the nurse that you have a migraine and want medication for its treatment\na Respond to the nurse's questions about your symptoms\n, Resist the idea of waiting for a doctor because you are convinced that you migraine and do not see\nthe point in waiting for 30 minutes\n, Be difficult to convince, but reluctantly agree to wait for a doctor\n\n@ET\n\nRole Player I URSING\nSETTING [emergency Room\nNURSE You are speaking to a 25-year old man/woman who has presented himself/herself\n\nHe/she looks very uncomfortable\n\nPASIS i Find out the reason for the patient's visit\na When the patient demands medication for migraine treatment, ask whether the patient has been\nclinically diagnosed with a migraine\n, lake a relevant history of the patient's condition (the type of pain, pain score, other symptoms\nExplain that he/she needs to see the doctor who would meet the patient after 30 minutes\nla Explain the risks involved in self-diagnosis/self-treatment\nr Emphasize the importance of getting a confirmed diagnosis from the doctor\n\nPrepared by SV & DM", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "SETTING Emergency Room\n\nPATIENT You are a 25-year-old man/woman suffering fre m a headache. You have been suffering from a left-sided\nheadache since yesterday. The pain is \"pounding\" and is accompanied by nausea and vomiting. You have\nincreased sensinvity to light and sound,\n\nOver-the-counter painkiller has not be